<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Plains of Abraham</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1759">1759</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Plains of Abraham was fought on 13 September 1759 outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> City between British forces under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-wolfe">James Wolfe</a> and French forces under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-joseph-de-montcalm">Marquis de Montcalm</a>. After climbing the cliffs above the St Lawrence by night, the British won in less than an hour; both commanders were mortally wounded. Quebec surrendered days later, and the battle led to the British conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-plains-of-abraham.jpg" alt="Battle of the Plains of Abraham" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benjamin West · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Benjamin_West_005.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
